===Etymology 1===
[[File:Goat 01.jpg|thumb|Domestic goat]]
[[File:PikiWiki Israel 38769 Male Ibex.jpg|thumb|[[Nubian ibex]] ({{taxlink|Capra nubiana|species}})]]

From {{inh|en|enm|goot}}, {{m|enm|got}}, {{m|enm|gat}}, from {{inh|en|ang|gāt}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*gait}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*gaits}}, from a {{der|en|qfa-sub}} language.

The sense of ''lecherous man'' derives from the slang expression "[[horny]] as a goat".

====Noun====
{{wikipedia}}
{{wikipedia|Capra (genus)}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q2934}}A mammal, {{taxfmt|Capra aegagrus hircus|subspecies}}, and similar species of the [[genus]] ''[[Capra]]''.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1980|title=AA book of British Villages|publisher=Drive Publications Ltd|page=164|text=The first thing that greets you on entering the church is a notice asking you not to vex the '''goat''', since it renders valuable service in keeping the churchyard tidy.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2025 February 5|author=Howard Johnston|title=Regional News: Southern|journal=RAIL|issue=1028|page=22|text=Folkestone: Network Rail and the White Cliffs Countryside Project have procured a herd of '''goats''' to keep vegetation on the slopes of Folkestone Warren under control, and to encourage rare species.}}
## {{lb|en|uncountable}} The meat of the aforementioned animal.
##: {{ux|en|Ugh, we're having '''goat''' for dinner again.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author={{w|Jesmyn Ward}}|title={{w|Where the Line Bleeds}}|publisher=Bloomsbury (2018)|page=157|passage=Joshua could not stop himself from scooping more '''goat''' on his plate: Paul had cooked it so long that the meat seemed to melt like hot, syrupy candy in his mouth. Joshua remembered '''goat''' as a stringy dark meat, but the red spicy mass before him was nothing like he recalled.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[lecherous]] [[man]].
# {{lb|en|informal}} A [[scapegoat]].
#* {{quote-text|en|date=Aug 6 2008|chapter=Tigers already miss Jones|title=Royal Oak Daily Tribune|location=Michigan
|passage=Fernando Rodney, the '''goat''' in Sunday's 10th inning loss to Tampa Bay, threw three nearly perfect innings in relief on Tuesday after being demoted from the closer role.}}
#* '''1997''', "{{w|1997 World Series}}", Game 7, bottom 11th inning, TV broadcast on NBC Sports, early morning October 27, 1997; words by Bob Costas
#*: Tony Fernández, who has worn hero's laurels throughout the postseason including earlier in this seventh game of the World Series, now cruel as it may seem, perhaps being fitted for '''goat''' horns.
# {{lb|en|slang}} A {{w|Pontiac GTO}} [[car]].
# {{lb|en|speech recognition}} A person who is not easily understood by a [[speech recognition]] system; contrasted with {{m|en|sheep}}.
# A [[fool]], [[loser]], or object of ridicule.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|title=Trusting Appearances: Things Are Not Always as They Seem |author=Ned B. Ricks |page=259 |ISBN=|passage=Samaurez said over his shoulder, “In fact, I missed being the class '''goat''' by only three places.” Gwen patted his arm, “But, look H-Two, George Pickett was the '''goat''' and see how famous he became.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013 |title=In Search of Butch Cassidy|author=Larry Pointer |page= |ISBN=|passage=...Butch was the '''goat''' in that deal and innocent of the trap he was placed in. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|title=The Octopus|author=Frank Norris |page= |ISBN=|passage=“If Osterman wants to play the '''goat''', why should you help him out?” }}
# {{lb|en|roller derby}} A [[blocker]] who is isolated behind the opposing team's blockers, so as to slow down the [[pack]].

